TinyX
=====

This is the TinyCore Linux TinyX source tree. The OpenSillicon port keeps the
machine-independent X11 server code and disables the BIOS-dependent Xvesa
backend. See PORTING.md for the imported revision and port status.


Why?
----

The TinyX servers fill our needs while being a lot smaller than Xorg can be made.


Design choices
--------------

We aim for a small X server. The upstream tree includes a Linux fbdev server;
it remains as reference code for the OpenSillicon framebuffer backend. The
VESA server is not part of this port.

- no xkb; it's bloat when console keymaps suffice
- no xinput
- no xinerama
- no gl
- TCP listening disabled by default, shadow FB enabled by default
...


Licensing
---------

While the original codebase is MIT, any changes here are GPLv3. Supporting closed devices
with this code is not a goal.

